# StreamForge: Distributed Python Event Processor

## 📌 Project Overview

**StreamForge** is a distributed real-time event processing system designed to ingest and process truck telemetry data using Apache Kafka and Python-based stream processing.

The system processes temperature readings generated from trucks, groups events into five-minute event-time windows, calculates aggregation statistics, maintains persistent state using RocksDB, provides state recovery through a Kafka changelog, and exposes monitoring metrics using Prometheus.

---

## 🎯 Problem Statement

Modern transportation systems generate a large amount of real-time telemetry data from connected vehicles. Processing this data efficiently requires a distributed system capable of handling continuous event streams, maintaining state, recovering from worker failures, and monitoring processing performance.

StreamForge addresses this requirement by building a distributed event-processing pipeline using Kafka, Python stream processing, RocksDB and Prometheus.

