# 📅 Week 3 – Stateful Recovery

## Objective

Week 3 focused on maintaining persistent processing state and recovering state after worker failures.

## RocksDB State Store

RocksDB was integrated as the local state store.

The state maintains aggregation information such as:

```text
window_start
count
sum
average
```

## Kafka Changelog

A Kafka topic named:

```text
aggregation-changelog
```

was used to store updated aggregation state.

The changelog provides durable state information that can be used during worker recovery.

## Worker Recovery

The recovery workflow is:

```text
Worker Processing
       ↓
RocksDB State
       ↓
Kafka Changelog
       ↓
Worker Failure
       ↓
Worker Restart
       ↓
Changelog Replay
       ↓
State Recovery
       ↓
Continue Processing
```

## Fault Tolerance Test

Two workers were configured using the same Kafka consumer group.

During testing:

1. Worker 1 was stopped intentionally.
2. Kafka redistributed available partitions.
3. Worker 2 continued processing.
4. Worker 1 was restarted.
5. Previous aggregation state was recovered.
6. Processing continued with the recovered state.

## Week 3 Result

The system successfully demonstrated persistent state management and recovery after worker failure.

